{
  "_doc": [
    "Hand-written scripted battles for move_effects_reference.rb (Ruby) and src/battle/move/moveEffectsReference.test.ts (TS).",
    "move_effects_reference.rb also adds one automatic scenario per move function code (see its header).",
    "p / o: the player's / opponent's party. Entry defaults: sp MEW, lv 40 (p) / 42 (o), m [TACKLE], g 0 (p) / 1 (o) (gender),",
    "  it (held item) none, ab (ability) HONEYGATHER, st (status) NONE, hp (fraction of total HP) 1.",
    "turns: one array per round, one action per battler index (0, 1, 2, 3): 'N' = move N (default target: first foe, or",
    "  first ally for ally-only moves), 'N>T' = move N at battler T, 'sN' = switch to party index N, null = move 0.",
    "  A move that can't be chosen falls back to the next choosable one (then Struggle).",
    "double: 2v2 (party entries 0 and 1 lead). trainer: the opponent is a trainer (lets the foe switch)."
  ],
